<title>SINGAPORE: Bangchak buys Jul MTBE from SABIC at around $260/T.</title>
<headline>Bangchak buys Jul MTBE from SABIC at around $260/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangchak Petroleum Plc has bought by tender 1,500-tonne of methyl tertiary butyl ether (MTBE) for delivery in first week of July at around $260 per tonne cost-and-freight (c+f) Bangkok, from Saudi Basic Industries Corp (SABIC), industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender for the gasoline octane-booster which closed June 16 and was valid for a day, received around five offers.</p>
<p>The award was slightly lower than Bangchak's last purchase, for June delivery, which was from domestic supplier Bangkok Synthetic at $265 per tonne, c+f Thailand.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
